 space of image features .In our experiments , f ( I ) is a 6 4 - dimensional feature vector produced by the last linear layer of a 3 4 - layer ResNet ( modified to accept 3 2 × 3 2 CIFAR images ) and g is a linear transformation .Fig. 5 compares chance performance ( 1/|U| ) , random vectors , GloVe , and GloVe+ViCo on four seen/unseen splits .The key conclusions are as follows : ViCo generalizes to unseen classes better than GloVe .ViCo based embeddings , especially 2 0 0 - dim .
